      "worked": "The perpendicular bisector passes through the midpoint and has the negative reciprocal of the joining line's gradient.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}M&=\\left(\\frac{1+3}{2},\\frac{4+8}{2}\\right)\\\\M&=(2,6)\\\\m_{PQ}&=\\frac{8-4}{3-1}\\\\m_{PQ}&=2\\\\m_{\\perp}&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing point–gradient form:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-6&=-\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)\\\\y-6&=-\\frac{1}{2}x+1\\\\y&=-\\frac{1}{2}x+7\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
